/* exists a. P(|a|) over the reals with P(x) the singleton x = -1: invalid, since |a| is never
   negative.  The optimizer's quantifier erasure once took |a| to be onto and answered valid.  (The
   .hes grammar has only the real absolute value, abs.; the integer one reaches the optimizer from
   other frontends.) */
exists (a: real). P (abs. a)
s.t.
P (x: real): bool =mu x = -1.0;
